label ym1:
    [   0] scene black
    [   1] with None
    [   2] scene bg club_day
    [   3] with Dissolve(2)
    [   4] # RenpyUnlock: Unlock { UnlockType=Normal, UnlockName="bgm_justalittlebit", UnlockId=2828920242 }
    [   5] play music "p5"
    [   6] show monika 2d at f21 zorder 3
    [   7] m "Am I bothering you?"
    [   8] show yuri 1e at f22 zorder 3
    [   9] y "Hm? No."
    [  10] m 2a "Okay, just checking. It's hard to tell since you always look so into it when you're reading. It makes me scared to interrupt."
    [  11] y 2i "Well, it's within my expectations to be interrupted when I read here. It's mainly when I'm by myself that I don't like it."
    [  12] m 2b "Mm, that makes sense. I guess if you're here in the first place, then you're more ready to socialize, even if it takes a little bit of prodding."
    [  13] y 2m "It's not so bad to be social if I let others do the work. So it can be healthy to put myself in a social environment every now and then."
    [  14] y 2h "It's mostly difficult when I don't know anyone, or there are too many people, or everyone is being too silly for me to keep up with..."
    [  15] show yuri at thide zorder 1
    [  16] hide yuri
    [  17] show monika at thide zorder 1
    [  18] hide monika
    [  19] "Yuri glances across the room at Sayori and Natsuki."
    [  20] "Sayori has her head cocked back and her mouth open, trying to catch pieces of a cookie that Natsuki is lobbing into the air, but the pieces keep bouncing off her face and hitting the floor."
    [  21] show monika 3n at f21 zorder 3
    [  22] m "Maybe I should say something..."
    [  23] show yuri 1k at f22 zorder 3
    [  24] y "No need, they just ran out of cookie. What a waste."
    [  25] m 2a "They've really become good friends, haven't they? I'm happy."
    [  26] y 2a "Sayori seems particularly good at making that happen..."
    [  27] y "But the two of them are both on the energetic side, so I suppose it works out well."
    [  28] m 3b "Yeah... Come to think of it, you and I haven't had many chances to talk one-on-one, have we?"
    [  29] m 3e "Though that may be partially my fault, since I'm supposed to be the one engaging club members."
    [  30] y 3j "Not at all..."
    [  31] y "I've probably formed a habit of drawing minimal attention to myself."
    [  32] y 3i "The responsibility is equally on me...at least to display some openness to engage."
    [  33] m 1d "Well, what about during times like lunch? Do you meet up with friends?"
    [  34] y 3v "I...I just read..."
    [  35] m 1f "Oh..."
    [  36] y 3t "...But I like it that way!"
    [  37] y 3u "It feels nice to be carried off again after a morning of classes..."
    [  38] m 2a "Hmm, do you always read fantasy?"
    [  39] y 1f "Oh, not always."
    [  40] y "I suppose it's all I've read recently, but only because I'm in the middle of this series."
    [  41] y "There are still two more books after this one."
    [  42] m 2j "I guess those long books suit you well, since you spend so much time reading."
    [  43] y 1i "Well, fantasy may be my favorite, but after that, I'm more or less indiscriminate to genres. I'll read anything with depth and maturity."
    [  44] m 2a "Oh yeah?"
    [  45] m 2j "Even like...romance?"
    [  46] y 3o "Well--!"
    [  47] y "There are a lot of books that...have elements of romance in them..."
    [  48] m 2k "Oh, come on, Yuri. You know what I mean."
    [  49] "Monika lowers her voice."
    [  50] m 5a "It's a guilty pleasure of mine, so I won't tell anyone if you do too."
    [  51] y 3g "..."
    [  52] y "Maybe...more when I was in middle school..."
    [  53] y 3q "I mean...I was really lonely, and people were mean to me a lot..."
    [  54] y "So I just... It kind of felt like..."
    [  55] y 4b "Ngh, please don't make me think about the past..."
    [  56] m "Hehe, sorry. I just got super curious."
    [  57] m 2a "You know...we should totally pick out a romance novel to read. That would be so much fun."
    [  58] y 3h "Absolutely not."
    [  59] m 2d "Really? Even if it was just between us?"
    [  60] y 1k "Try asking someone who has no shame. Like Natsuki."
    [  61] m 1l "Ouch..."
    [  62] y 3o "Ah--S-Sorry...I swear I didn't mean that..."
    [  63] m 2e "Well, I guess it was my fault for pressing you. I'm like that for things in my past, too...you know, things I feel too embarrassed to re-experience."
    [  64] y 2h "There's nothing wrong with growing out of things. It happens to everyone."
    [  65] y 2j "For instance, Natsuki's interest in manga reminds me quite a bit of how intense I used to be about my own interests."
    [  66] y "It makes me think that she'll likely grow out of it, too."
    [  67] show monika 2e at t31 zorder 2
    [  68] show yuri 2j at t32 zorder 2
    [  69] show natsuki 2k at f33 zorder 3
    [  70] n "Hey, were you talking about me?"
    [  71] y 3o "Um-- No, we were just--"
    [  72] m 2b "Oh, we were just talking about how our interests have changed over the years."
    [  73] m "When did you get into manga, Natsuki?"
    [  74] n 2j "Hm? Like a couple years ago, I guess."
    [  75] n "I was already sort of into it before that, but I wasn't really going hard until then."
    [  76] m 2a "Oh yeah? What was it that inspired you to get more into it?"
    [  77] n 2c "I dunno."
    [  78] n "I guess...let me think..."
    [  79] n 2d "It was after I discovered a series that I really liked."
    [  80] n 4y "Yeah, I was just like...really fed up with a lot of things, and I got super into this one series that I really related to."
    [  81] n "I guess I had an edgy phase where I just hated everyone around me and wanted to be by myself. Ahaha!"
    [  82] m 2k "Hey, kind of like Yuri!"
    [  83] y 3n "M-Monika!"
    [  84] m 2j "Ahaha, sorry..."
    [  85] y 2h "That's...completely wrong, so..."
    [  86] m 3b "It's still cool that you both really found your thing."
    [  87] m "They're almost like opposites, but it sounds like they helped you a lot through hard times."
    [  88] n 4d "You know it."
    [  89] y 1v "Mm..."
    [  90] n 2l "Wow, what the heck? Is that book even bigger than the last one you were reading?"
    [  91] y 3q "Ah...um..."
    [  92] y "It's...technically slightly longer, but not by very much."
